{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, I'm Dr. Patel. I'll be your doctor during your stay. You were brought in because your blood sugar was extremely high. Can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, last night my glucose monitor said 'does not register.' It's been running between 200 and 500 since I left the hospital a couple of weeks ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You’re on Lantus at bedtime and Humalog with meals, correct? Any changes to your diet or medications?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No changes. I’m still taking everything the same. I’ve been eating okay, maybe a bit more since I started Megace for my appetite."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That might be part of the issue. Megace can make your body more resistant to insulin, which raises blood sugar. We also saw your kidney function is a bit worse than usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My kidneys again? They’ve always been bad since the transplant."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your creatinine is 2.2, up from your usual 1.5. But it improved to 1.6 after fluids in the ER. This looks like it’s due to dehydration from high sugars causing you to urinate a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I have been going to the bathroom a lot. I thought it was the Megace."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could be both. High glucose spills into the urine and pulls water with it. That also explains why your potassium was high at first — your kidneys weren’t clearing it well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous? My potassium?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was 7.2 initially, which is concerning, but it corrected to 5.5 after fluids and no EKG changes. It’s now normal. So we’re watching it, but it’s improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. What about my insulin? I don’t want to go into a coma or anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No signs of ketoacidosis or coma. You’re alert and your labs don’t show that. But we do need to adjust your insulin. The endocrine team recommends increasing your Lantus from 3 units to 10 units at bedtime."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a big jump! Won’t I go low?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor closely. You’ve been running very high, so this is to bring you into a safer range. We’ll also adjust your Humalog sliding scale to give more insulin when your sugar is high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. And what about the Megace? I finally have an appetite."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to cut it in half — from 20 mL to 10 mL daily. It’s likely contributing to the insulin resistance. We’ll see how your appetite does on the lower dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can try that. Will I lose weight again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2196-11-08 04:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll watch that. The transplant team will help manage your nutrition. For now, the priority is getting your sugars under control safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2196-11-08 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your fingerstick this morning is 385. Still high, but we expected that. We’ve increased your Lantus to 10 units last night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2196-11-08 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s not dropping fast, is it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2196-11-08 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It takes a few days to stabilize. Your A1c was 7.3%, which shows your average sugar has been high over the last few months. We’re on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2196-11-08 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been trying. It’s just hard with all these meds and my stomach issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2196-11-08 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’re keeping your other medications the same — tacrolimus, mycophenolate, mirtazapine for depression and appetite, and your blood pressure medicine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2196-11-08 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, I just checked my sugar — it’s 410. Should I take extra Humalog?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2196-11-08 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, according to your new sliding scale, you should take 8 units of Humalog now. We’ve adjusted the scale to be more aggressive."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2196-11-08 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll do that. I’m just worried I’m not doing enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2196-11-08 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. This is a process. Your sugars will come down as the new doses take effect. We’re also watching your kidney function and electrolytes daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2196-11-09 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your labs look better. Creatinine is down to 1.6, potassium is 4.9, and your glucose this morning was 290 — still high, but trending down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2196-11-09 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good! Is the new insulin working?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2196-11-09 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s starting to. We’ll keep the Lantus at 10 units and further adjust your Humalog scale today to help with mealtime spikes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2196-11-09 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the half-dose Megace? I’m still eating okay so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2196-11-09 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great news. The transplant team wants you to keep it at 10 mL and follow up with them to monitor your intake and weight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2196-11-09 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, I feel much better. My sugars are staying around 280-300. Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2196-11-09 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s improving. We’d like to see it under 200 eventually, but this is progress. Your kidney function is stable, and you’re not having any symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2196-11-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — you’re ready to go home today. Your sugars are more stable, and your labs are improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2196-11-10 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great! What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2196-11-10 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue the new insulin: 10 units Lantus at bedtime, and use the updated Humalog sliding scale. Take half your Megace — 10 mL daily. Keep all your other meds the same."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2196-11-10 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my follow-ups?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2196-11-10 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See the endocrine clinic tomorrow, your transplant team soon, and we’ll help you set up with a new primary care doctor. You’re doing well — just keep monitoring your sugars."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2196-11-10 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much more in control now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2196-11-10 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Call if your sugars go too high or too low. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2196-11-08 04:13:00",
    "admission_end": "2196-11-10 18:41:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 72-year-old woman with a history of liver transplant for HCV cirrhosis, type 2 diabetes, and chronic kidney disease was admitted for severe hyperglycemia with glucose levels exceeding 500 and glucosuria. She reported poor glycemic control since her last discharge, attributed to increased oral intake and ongoing use of megestrol, which can induce insulin resistance. Initial labs showed acute on chronic renal failure with a creatinine of 2.2, likely prerenal due to osmotic diuresis, and hyperkalemia (K+ 7.2) that resolved with fluid resuscitation. The endocrine team recommended intensifying insulin therapy, increasing her Lantus dose from 3 to 10 units at bedtime and adjusting her Humalog sliding scale. Megace was reduced from 20 mL to 10 mL daily to mitigate insulin resistance. Over the hospital stay, her glucose levels trended downward, kidney function improved, and electrolytes normalized. She was discharged home with updated insulin and Megace dosing, and plans for close follow-up with endocrinology, transplant, and primary care teams.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with ophthalmic manifestations, type II or unspecified type, uncontrolled",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Background diabetic retinopathy",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Need for prophylactic vaccination and inoculation against influenza",
      "Liver replaced by transplant",
      "Chronic kidney disease, unspecified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, without mention of intractable epilepsy",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Essential and other specified forms of tremor",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of liver"
    ]
  }
}
